:name: DeltaVR two-board simulation
:description: Headset (deltavr_hmd) + controller (deltavr_controller) nice!nano
:            boards, running together with I2C sensor stubs and an nRF24L01
:            SPI bridge between them.
:
: Run from the deltavirtual folder:
:   renode run_two_boards.resc

using sysbus

# Custom peripherals, shared across both machines in this Renode process.
i @renode/peripherals/UICRStub.cs
i @renode/peripherals/NRF24L01Stub.cs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Headset board (deltavr_hmd.kicad_sch): nice!nano + LSM6DSVTR + nRF24L01
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
mach create "headset"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/platforms/nicenano_deltavr.repl

sysbus.nrf24 NodeId "headset"
include @renode/peripherals/lsm6dsv_i2c_stub.py

showAnalyzer uart0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Controller board (deltavr_controller.kicad_sch): nice!nano + LSM6DSVTR +
# ADS1115 (hall sensors + joystick) + nRF24L01
#
# deltavr_controller.elf is currently a copy of the deltavirtual sample
# firmware (UART printk loop) so the second machine boots. Replace it with
# your real controller build when you have one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
mach create "controller"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/platforms/nicenano_deltavr.repl

sysbus.nrf24 NodeId "controller"
include @renode/peripherals/lsm6dsv_i2c_stub.py
include @renode/peripherals/ads1115_i2c_stub.py

showAnalyzer uart0

# Load ELFs on every machine reset (nRF52840 does SYSRESETREQ during boot).
macro reset
"""
    mach set "headset"
    sysbus LoadELF @renode/firmware/deltavr_hmd.elf

    mach set "controller"
    sysbus LoadELF @renode/firmware/deltavr_controller.elf
"""
runMacro $reset

start
